A||||17||Berserk||Why a Fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||Berserk||10-11-2001||10:43 PM||||I'm looking for a car to replace my '86 Trans Am pretty soon.  It needs to serve as a daily driver, but since I'm in college, I don't need to worry about carrying people much.  What I'm really wondering about with the Fiero is how much luggage capacity they really have.  I don't have much to take places, but I would like to be able to go visit people or maybe take my girlfriend for a weekend trip.  How are you all making out with your's?<P>I'm looking for an '87 GT, 5spd||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-11-2001||10:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Berserk:<BR><B>How are you all making out with your's?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>well, you go to a quiet spot, shut off the car.. oh wait, that's not what you meant.. is it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Fieros will carry more than you'd suspect, I've heard of a set of golf clubs fitting in the trunk.. I wouldn't want to ever have to move with a Fiero though, but for a couple of overnight bags (for a weekend trip) should be fine..<P>welcome to the forum..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Hank is Here||10-11-2001||11:16 PM||||I can carry an amazing amount in my Fiero.  You get used to using every nook and cranny of the car. There is the true truck and even some room up front.  then if you slide the seats forward a little there is some room ther for hangning bags.  <BR>I always carrs  Sears 101 piece tool set, folding shovel, canteen, set of wrenches, grease gun, jumper cables, and still have nothing in the trunk!   I really never use any of the stuff but it doesn't get in the way at all||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackStang95||10-12-2001||12:35 AM||||There is a fair amount of storage space...it is oddly shaped in my opinion (deep and narrow), but if you pack well I think weekend trips are no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||10-12-2001||01:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Why a Fiero?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR><I>Why not?</I>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo.jpg">  <BR><B><I><FONT SIZE="2"><FONT COLOR="blue">My7Fieros</B></I></FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroFanaticus2||10-12-2001||07:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B> <BR>I wouldn't want to ever have to move with a Fiero <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I used the fiero to help move a while back, You can actually fit A LOT of packed boxes in the passenger seat, and set tons of loose stuff in the rear storage compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000006||kyote||10-12-2001||07:31 AM||||If you are going to be going off for a weekend with the girlfriend.. <BR>Who needs luggage..???<BR><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE<BR>'84 SE (Strictly Parts Car)<BR>'86 SE||||reg||12
Z||000007||Old Lar||10-12-2001||08:06 AM||||Hulkie designd the Fiero trunk to hold two golf bags, hence deep and narrow. Pack with duffle bags, no problem for traveling.  For longer trips, use the local laudromat to catch up with the clean cloths.   As for making out with your GF in a Fiero, you need to be limber.||||reg||1
Z||000008||grinthock||10-12-2001||08:50 AM||||I can fit just about as much stuff in my fiero as most cars if you get smart...  I was for awhile running without a spare tire.  So I had even MORE room, but even with teh spare in (up frnot) I can store a LARGE backpack up front, pull the spare and you can pack that compartment FULL of stuff<P>The passenger seat can hold ALOT of stuff on the floor and the seat itself and the trunk IF you measure it is close to the size of the trunk in a Honda CIVIC just oriented differently.||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||10-12-2001||09:56 AM||||i've got a friend with an 87 GT, runs killer looks awsome.. OZ wheels.. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/005018.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/005018.html</A> <P>Worth every penny...<P>I beat the <B>CRAP</B> out of my cars and they seem VERY tough! been spraying goobs of nitrous, and driving it like its stolen for years and it's still stomping nuts. <P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||10-12-2001||11:45 AM||||I can fit only one bag of golf clubs in the back. I don't see a way to stuff two unless you take the clubs out. But, this car can be stuffed pretty well. No complaint on that.||||reg||1
Z||000011||pHoOl||10-12-2001||11:53 AM||||I also am i college student, and lemme tell you, these things can hold a LOT!!.  When i go home for Christmas, i take home my Sony Hometheater system with power subwoofer, receiver, computer, monitor, large laundry basket, pots and pans, all my dirty laundry.  I know that i am fogetting a lot of stuff.... but basically anything that you would wnat to get out of your room or apartment so it doesn't get stolen over a break, i take home in the fiero.  Granted, it's stuffed to the gills, but i can still see out of every window and every mirror.  No room for a passenger though.<P>If you want to take your girl on a trip... like they said, pack the back with backpacks, you could prolly fit 3 or 4 large bags of clothes back there<P>I never thought i could carry as much as i can in it!<P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||10-12-2001||12:55 PM||||These things can be stuffed with a lot of stuff!  But be careful... a gf on a weekend trip with you can bring an AWFUL lot of stuff.  On a weekend trip, a past gf packed the trunk of my Probe FULL of all kinds of bags  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  For 4 days!!  Now being a hatchback the trunk can swallow a ton of stuff!  A U-haul might be more your liking if you take a lot of trips with the gf.<P>Back to Fieros... they will hold a ton in the trunk with some smart packing!  For hauling/moving, it isn't totally useless.  I brought a 10,000 BTU window air conditioner home in the passenger seat.  It wasn't an easy fit, but the salesman and I unboxed it and managed to get it in there!  As for a daily driver... as long as you won't be going thru deep snow often you will be fine.  I'd definately recommend one.||||reg||1
Z||000013||85ZainoGT||10-12-2001||04:37 PM||||im sellin mine for $2200, and buying another to build up if your interested..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000014||Smoooooth GT||10-12-2001||05:18 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Hank is Here:<BR>folding shovel ??QUOTE]<BR>:d COOL, I can dig that idea..   <P>REAL REASON:   to make it Smooooth...  <BR>Welcome to the Forum...    Steve<P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L V/6<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Mattyman||10-12-2001||11:14 PM||||The Fiero is excelent with luggage and stuff.  Its bigger than most peolple suspect.  Im a college student too and I can fit alot of stuff in the trunk.  I drive my friend up and back with me sometimes and we can fit like 2 big bags full of laundry 3 bookbags, shoes and alot of other crap in the trunk.  My golf clubs also fit in the back perfectly with room to spare.  Sometimes i cut grass for a friend of mine and a few times i had to put a weekwacker in the front pasenger seat. I make sure its all covered though, dont want to get the interior dirty.  But over all the Fiero is a good choice.||||reg||1
Z||000016||theogre||10-13-2001||04:05 PM||||I had the tire off my minivan in the back of mine last week. Still had room for my floor jack and stuff. Couldn't quite shut the lid once the tire was aired up after it was fixed.<P>It's still big enough that 1 or 2 kids can get into it and shut the lid. One of the reasons I worked out an alternate for the power trunk release's 12V source. Also keeps people out of trunk when the windows/doors are left open/unlocked...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000017||BN Boomer||10-13-2001||06:39 PM||||Fieros do carry more than you would expect, but it still ain't all that much. You'll do just fine on weekend trips, but you're pretty much screwed if you have to transport large or bulky items at all. The luggage rack is a joke, don't plan on getting much if any use out of it. I would say that if you tend to travel light and pack efficiently, you'll find the Fiero has ample room for the basics. <P>I've found that a radiator from a Suburban can just barely be squeezed into the front passenger seat/foot well.||||reg||1
